# The one account on the device besides root (security review
# 2026-09-11, M8). Buildroot's users table:
#
#   username uid group gid password home shell groups comment
#
# uid and gid are written out rather than left to Buildroot, because
# /etc/mdev.conf and the vfat mount in /etc/init.d/rcS name the same
# numbers and two builders must get the same bytes.
#
# The password is "*", which no password matches, so the account cannot
# be logged into even on the dev variant's serial console. The home is
# "-", which means "/" and no directory of its own: the app writes to the
# card and nowhere else. The shell is /bin/false.
opensigner 200 opensigner 200 * - /bin/false - the account the app runs as
